<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/undated">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Carrhae</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Carrhae · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-parthian-wars">Roman–Parthian Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Carrhae was fought in 53 BCE near Carrhae (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harran">Harran</a>) in upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>. A Parthian army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horse-archer">horse archers</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heavy-cavalry">heavy cavalry</a> under the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/surena">Surena</a> destroyed a Roman army led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-licinius-crassus">Marcus Licinius Crassus</a>, who was killed. It was one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>'s worst defeats and established the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthian-empire">Parthian Empire</a> as Rome's great rival in the east.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-carrhae.jpg" alt="Battle of Carrhae" width="320" height="215" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Theodore Ayrault Dodge · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Carrhae_(Caesar%CB%90_A_History_Of_The_Art_Of_War_Among_The_Romans_Down_To_The_End,_vol._II,_1892).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
